==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang}} {{term|rihtwis|rihtwīs}}, corresponding to {{compound|right|wise}} (with assimilation of second element to {{term|-ous}}).

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ˈraɪtʃəs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-righteous.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|aɪtʃəs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[free]] from [[sin]] or [[guilt]]
# [[moral]] and [[virtuous]], suggesting [[sanctimonious]]
# [[justified]] [[morally]]
# (''slang US'') [[awesome]]

====Derived terms====
* [[righteousness]]
* [[self-righteous]]

